---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  description="Read about Toolsiva's accessibility approach, supported interactions and issue reporting."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 lg:py-16">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-brand-300">Accessibility</p>
    <h1 class="mt-2 text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl">
      Building tools that are easier to use
    </h1>
    <div class="prose-premium mt-10 space-y-10 text-sm leading-7 text-zinc-300">
      <section><h2>Our approach</h2><p>Toolsiva aims to support keyboard navigation, visible focus indicators, semantic HTML, clear labels, readable contrast, responsive layouts and understandable status feedback.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Keyboard interaction</h2><p>Primary navigation, form fields, buttons, links and expandable sections are intended to work without a mouse. A skip link is provided to move directly to main content.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Responsive presentation</h2><p>Layouts adapt for desktop, tablet and mobile screens. Complex two-column workspaces collapse into a single-column flow on smaller displays.</p></section>
      <section><h2>Known limitations</h2><p>Native date inputs, canvases, generated QR images, code editors and browser-specific controls can vary between assistive technologies. Toolsiva is actively reviewing these areas.</p></section>
      <section>
        <h2>Report an accessibility issue</h2>
        <p>
          Send the page URL, browser, operating system, assistive technology and a description
          of the problem to{" "}
          <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
